  "title": "Restoration of the Oka River’s upper estuary, part of the Urdaibai Biosphere Reserve, Spain",
  "summary": "The Oka River estuary in Spain faces landscape changes from human activities and climate threats. Restoration efforts aim to enhance resilience to climate impacts, increase biodiversity, and promote sustainable public use. Activities involve recovering marshlands, removing barriers, constructing lagoons, and eradicating invasive species. The estuary of the Oka River is located within the Urdaibai Biosphere Reserve, on the coast of Biscay, Basque Country, north of Spain. It is an area of high ecological value. Its landscape has been transformed over the years by human activities, as it has been inhabited since Prehistoric times.",
